    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0046_931b69da4118.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 105px;\" /><br /><br /><math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br /><math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math><br /><br />In this compound, the heavier groups attached to the double bonded carbon atoms are at the opposite side, so the configuration of second carbon is E.<br /><br />The fourth carbon can be represent as<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0046_031bda12f445.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 125px;\" /><br /><br />Priority for <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> configuration,<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mtext>&nbsp;group</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math><br /><br />Since, the least prior group is attached to solid line, the clockwise <math><mn>1</mn><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>→</mo><mn>3</mn></math> rotation gives S-configuration."
